      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/basalto-olivinico-alcalino",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/basalto"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Basalto olivínico subsaturado en sílice, caracterizado por la ausencia de ortopiroxeno y cuarzo y por la presencia de olivino, así como de feldespatoide, feldespato alcalino o flogopita en la matriz. los fenocristales de feldespato varían de labradorita a andesina. la augita es rica en titanio en comparación con la augita de los basaltos toleíticos. el basalto olivínico alcalino es relativamente rico en sodio."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Alkali olivine basalt is silica-undersaturated, characterized by the absence of orthopyroxene, absence of quartz, presence of olivine, and typically contains some feldspathoid mineral, alkali feldspar or phlogopite in the groundmass. feldspar phenocrysts typically are labradorite to andesine in composition. augite is rich in titanium compared to augite in tholeiitic basalt. alkali olivine basalt is relatively rich in sodium."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/alkaliOlivineBasalt"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/alkali-olivine_basalt"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "basalto olivínico alcalino"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "alkali olivine basalt"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/fonolitoide",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-afanitica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca volcánica que contiene menos de un 90 por ciento de minerales máficos y entre un 10 y un 60 por ciento de feldespatoide entre los componentes qapf. su proporción de plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato es inferior al 50 por ciento. incluye a las rocas de los sectores 11 y 12 del diagrama qapf y a las del sector ph en el diagrama tas."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Fine grained igneous rock than contains less than 90 percent mafic minerals, between 10 and 60 percent feldspathoid mineral in the qapf fraction and has a plagioclase to total feldspar ratio less than 0.5. includes rocks defined modally in qapf fields 11 and 12, and tas field ph."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/phonolitoid"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/phonolitoid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/fonolita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/fonolita-tefritica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "fonolitoide"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "phonolitoid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
