      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "monzogranite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-dolomitico-impuro",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-dolomitico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Sedimento carbonatado en el que entre el 50 y el 90 por ciento de los elementos integrantes están compuestos por uno (o más) carbonatos de origen intracuencal, con una relación entre dolomita y calcita (incluyendo el aragonito) superior a 1."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carbonate sediment in which between 50 and 90 percent of the constituents are composed of one (or more) of the carbonate minerals in particles of intrabasinal origin, and the ratio of magnesium carbonate to calcite (plus aragonite) greater than 1 to 1."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/impureDolomiticSediment"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/impure_dolomitic_sediment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "sedimento dolomítico impuro"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "impure dolomitic sediment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-alcalina-exotica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-de-composicion-exotica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Kimberlita, lamproíta o lamprófido. generalmente son rocas potásicas máficas o ultramáficas. su contenido en olivino (frecuentemente serpentinizado en la kimberlita) y en flogopita es significativo."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kimberlite, lamproite, or lamprophyre. generally are potassic, mafic or ultramafic rocks. olivine (commonly serpentinized in kimberlite), and phlogopite are significant constituents."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/exoticAlkalineRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_alkaline_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca alcalina exótica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "exotic alkaline rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-poligenico",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-compuesto"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material con un estado de consolidación no especificado formado por modificación geológica de materiales preexistentes fuera del ámbito de los procesos ígneos y sedimentarios."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Material of unspecified consolidation state formed by geological modification of pre-existing materials outside the realm of igneous and sedimentary processes."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/compositeGenesisMaterial"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/composite_genesis_material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-poligenica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-relacionado-con-una-falla"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-generado-por-un-impacto"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/alterita"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "material poligénico"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "composite genesis material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-igneo-fragmentario",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-igneo"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material ígneo con un estado de consolidación no especificado formado en más del 75 por ciento por fragmentos resultantes de un proceso ígneo."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Igneous material of unspecified consolidation state in which greater than 75 percent of the rock consists of fragments produced as a result of igneous rock-forming process."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/fragmentalIgneousMaterial"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/fragmental_igneous_material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-fragmentaria"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-piroclastico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "material ígneo fragmentario"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "fragmental igneous material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-riolitica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-acida"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca volcánica compuesta por cuarzo y feldespato alcalino, con presencia de plagioclasa y biotita en una  matriz microcristalina, criptocristalina o vítrea. es habitual la textura fluidal. contiene menos del 90 por ciento de minerales máficos y, en relación con sus componentes del diagrama qapf, entre un 20 y un 60 por ciento de cuarzo, así como un contenido de plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato inferior al 65 por ciento. engloba a las rocas incluidas modalmente en los sectores 2 y 3 del diagrama qapf, así como las incluidas químicamente en el sector r del diagrama tas."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Fine grained igneous rock consisting of quartz and alkali feldspar, with minor plagioclase and biotite, in a microcrystalline, cryptocrystalline or glassy groundmass. flow texture is common. includes rocks defined modally in qapf fields 2 and 3 or chemically in tas field r as rhyolite. qapf normative definition is based on modal mineralogy thus: less than 90 percent mafic minerals, between 20 and 60 percent quartz in the qapf fraction, and ratio of plagioclse to total feldspar is less than 0.65."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/rhyolitoid"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/rhyolitoid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/riolita-de-feldespato-alcalino"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/riolita"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca riolítica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "rhyolitoid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/grauvaca",
    "@type": [
