        "@value": "roca ígnea vítrea"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "glassy igneous rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-dolomitico-puro",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-dolomitico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Sedimento carbonatado con más del 90 por ciento de sus constituyentes compuestos por uno (o más) carbonatos de origen intracuencal y con una proporción entre dolomita y calcita (incluido el aragonito) mayor que 1."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carbonate sediment in which greater than 90 percent of the constituents are composed of one (or more) of the carbonate minerals in particles of intrabasinal origin, and a ratio of magnesium carbonate to calcite (plus aragonite) greater than 1 to 1."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/pureDolomiticSediment"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/pure_dolomitic_sediment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "sedimento dolomítico puro"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "pure dolomitic sediment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-rica-en-materia-organica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario-rico-en-materia-organica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria cuyo color, composición, textura y densidad aparente indican que contiene más del 50 por ciento en peso (en seco) de materia orgánica."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary rock with color, composition, texture and apparent density indicating greater than 50 percent organic content by weight on a moisture-free basis."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/organicRichSedimentaryRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/organic_rich_sedimentary_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/carbon"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca rica en materia orgánica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "organic rich sedimentary rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario-ferruginoso",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario-quimico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material sedimentario en un estado de consolidación sin especificar  compuesto, al menos en un 50 por ciento, por minerales con hierro (hematites, magnetita, grupo de la limonita, siderita, sulfuros de hierro) determinados mediante lupa o análisis petrográfico. generalmente contiene un 15 por ciento de hierro en peso."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary material of unspecified consolidation state that consists of at least 50 percent iron-bearing minerals (hematite, magnetite, limonite-group, siderite, iron-sulfides), as determined by hand-lens or petrographic analysis. corresponds to a rock typically containing 15 percent iron by weight."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/ironRichSedimentaryMaterial"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/iron_rich_sedimentary_material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-ferruginoso"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimetaria-ferruginosa"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "material sedimentario ferruginoso"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "iron rich sedimentary material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/grainstone",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-carbonatada"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria carbonatada con matriz original reconocible, grano-soportada, constituida fundamentalmente por aloquímicos y sin matriz micrítica. se diferencia de las areniscas por el carácter intracuencal de sus clastos y por su fábrica grano-soportada, pero la definición de grainstone no contempla el criterio del tamaño de grano."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carbonate sedimentary rock with recognizable depositional fabric that is grain-supported, and constituent particles are of intrabasinal origin; contains little or no mud matrix. distinction from sandstone is based on interpretation of intrabasinal origin of clasts and grain-supported fabric, but grainstone definition does not include a grain size criteria."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/grainstone"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/grainstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "grainstone"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "grainstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/lignito",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/carbon"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Carbón consolidado, sin brillo, de marrón suave a negro, en el que pueden distinguirse fragmentos de plantas en una matriz orgánica de grano fino. incluye a todos los carbones de bajo rango, incluido el carbón sub-bituminoso, cuyas vetas marrones permiten su distinción con respecto al carbón bituminoso, de vetas negras. tiende a fracturarse al secarse. tiene un poder calorífico inferior a 24mj/kg (determinado según la iso 1928) y la reflectancia de la vitrinita es inferior al 0,6 por ciento (determinada según la iso 7404-5). el valor calorífico bruto se recalcula libre de cenizas y humedad usando la humedad inherente (determinado según la iso 1015 o la iso 5068)."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Coal that has a gross calorific value less than 24 mj/kg (determined in conformance with iso 1928), and vitrinite mean random reflectance less than 0.6 por ciento (determined in conformance with iso 7404-5). gross calorific value is recalculated to a moist, ash free basis using bed moisture (determined according to iso 1015 or iso 5068). includes all low-rank coals, including sub-bitiminous coal. a consolidated, dull, soft brown to black coal having many readily discernible plant fragments set in a finer grained organic matrix. tends to crack and fall apart on drying. operationally sub-bituminous and bitiminous coal are qualitatively distinguished based on brown streak for sub-bitiminous coal and black streak for bituminous coal."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/lignite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/lignite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "lignito"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "lignite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-carbonatada-pura",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-carbonatada"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria en la cual más de un 90 por ciento de sus constituyentes primarios o recristalizados son carbonatos."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary rock in which greater than 90 percent of the primary and/or recrystallized constituents are carbonate minerals."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/pureCarbonateSedimentaryRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/pure_carbonate_sedimentary_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca sedimentaria carbonatada pura"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "pure carbonate sedimentary rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-igneo-basico",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-igneo"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material ígneo con un contenido de sio2 entre el 45 y el 52 por ciento."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Igneous material with between 45 and 52 percent sio2."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/basicIgneousMaterial"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/basic_igneous_material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-basica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "material ígneo básico"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "basic igneous material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/diamicton",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-clastico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Sedimento clástico sin selección o mal seleccionado, de granulometría muy variada, con matriz lutítica. no incluye a los materiales biogénicos que tienen la misma textura. se diferencia de los conglomerados, las areniscas y las lutitas por la polimodalidad y la ausencia de estructuras relacionadas con su transporte y depósito por acción del aire o del agua. su denominación puede complementarse con la granulometría predominante."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Unsorted or poorly sorted, clastic sediment with a wide range of particle sizes, including a muddy matrix. biogenic materials that have such texture are excluded. distinguished from conglomerate, sandstone, mudstone based on polymodality and lack of structures related to transport and deposition of sediment by moving air or water. assignment to an other size class can be used in conjunction to indicate the dominant grain size."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/diamicton"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/diamicton"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "diamictón"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "diamicton"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-monzodioritica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/dioritoide"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Dioritoide con una proporción de plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato inferior al 90 por ciento. está compuesta por plagioclasa sódica (an0 a an50), feldespato alcalino, hornblenda y biotita, con ausencia o muy bajo contenido de piroxeno y hasta un 10 por ciento de feldespatoide o hasta un 20 por ciento de cuarzo entre los componentes qapf. incluye a las rocas de los sectores 9, 9' y 9* del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Phaneritic crystalline igneous rock consisting of sodic plagioclase (an0 to an50), alkali feldspar, hornblende and biotite, with or without pyroxene, and 0 to 10 percent feldspathoid or 0 to 20 percent quartz in the qapf fraction. plagioclase to total feldspar ratio in the qapf fraction is between 0.65 and 0.9. includes rocks defined modally in qapf field 9, 9' and 9* as monzodiorite, foid-bearing monzodiorite, and quartz monzodiorite."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/monzodioriticRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/monzodioritic_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/monzodiorita-con-foides"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/monzodiorita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/cuarzo-monzodiorita"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca monzodiorítica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "monzodioritic rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
