  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/diorita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-dioritica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca diorítica que contiene cuarzo en una proporción inferior al 5 por ciento, entre los componentes qapf. está compuesta por plagioclasa intermedia, comúnmente con horblenda y de manera frecuente con biotita o augita; contiene plagioclasa sódica (an0-an50). su índice de color m es inferior a 90. incluye a las rocas modalmente asignadas al campo 10 del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Phaneritic crystalline rock consisting of intermediate plagioclase, commonly with hornblende and often with biotite or augite; colour index m less than 90, sodic plagioclase (an0-an50), no feldspathoid, and between 0 and 5 percent quartz. includes rocks defined modally in qapf field 10 as diorite."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/diorite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/diorite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "diorita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "diorite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/basalto",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-basica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca volcánica porfídica o de grano fino con menos de un 20 por ciento de cuarzo y menos de un 10 por ciento de feldespatoide, entre los componentes qapf; la proporción de la plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato es mayor del 65 por ciento. generalmente está constituida por fenocristales de plagioclasa cálcica, clinopiroxeno y olivino. incluye a las rocas de los sectores 9 y 10 del diagrama qapf y del sector b del diagrama tas. el basalto y la andesita se diferencian químicamente por su contenido en sílice, siendo el del basalto inferior al 52 por ciento de su peso. si no se dispone de la composición química, se clasifican a partir del índice de color, en cuyo caso el basalto se define por contener más de un 35 por ciento de minerales máficos en volumen o más del 40 por ciento en peso."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Fine-grained or porphyritic igneous rock with less than 20 percent quartz, and less than 10 percent feldspathoid minerals, in which the ratio of plagioclase to total feldspar is greater 0.65. typically composed of calcic plagioclase and clinopyroxene; phenocrysts typically include one or more of calcic plagioclase, clinopyroxene, orthopyroxene, and olivine. includes rocks defined modally in qapf fields 9 and 10 or chemically in tas field b as basalt. basalt and andesite are distinguished chemically based on silica content, with basalt defined to contain less than 52 weight percent silica. if chemical data are not available, the color index is used to distinguish the categories, with basalt defined to contain greater than 35 percent mafic minerals by volume or greater than 40 percent mafic minerals by weight."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/basalt"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/basalt"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/basalto-olivinico-alcalino"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/basalto-toleitico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "basalto"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "basalt"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sieno-granito",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/granito"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Granito cuyo contenido en plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato es inferior al 35 por ciento. incluye a las rocas del sector 3a del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Granite that has a plagioclase to total feldspar ratio between 0.10 and 0.35. qapf field 3a."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/syenogranite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/syenogranite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "sieno-granito"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "syenogranite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/arenita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/arenisca"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Arenisca clástica que contiene menos del 10 por ciento de matriz. la matriz es de origen detrítico o diagenético y está formada por silicatos de tamaño lutita (arcilla, feldespatos, cuarzo, fragmentos de roca y productos de alteración)."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Clastic sandstone that contains less than 10 percent matrix. matrix is mud-size silicate minerals (clay, feldspar, quartz, rock fragments, and alteration products) of detrital or diagenetic nature."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/arenite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/arenite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "arenita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "arenite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
