  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/dolomia",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-dolomitica-o-magnesica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria carbonatada pura, con una relación entre dolomita y calcita (incluyendo el aragonito) mayor que 1."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Pure carbonate sedimentary rock with a ratio of magnesium carbonate to calcite (plus aragonite) greater than 1 to 1."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/dolomite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/dolostone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "dolomía"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "dolomite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/monzonita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-monzogabroica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca monzonítica con cuarzo en una proporción inferior al 5 por ciento, entre los componentes qapf. incluye a las rocas del sector 8 del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Monzonitic rock that contains 0-5 percent quartz and no feldspathoid mineral in the qapf fraction. includes rocks defined modally in qapf field 8."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/monzonite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/monzonite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "monzonita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "monzonite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario-quimico",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material sedimentario constituido al menos en el 50 por ciento por material producido por procesos químicos inorgánicos dentro de la cuenca de sedimentación. incluye sedimentos inorgánicos silíceos, carbonatados, evaporíticos, ferruginosos y fosfáticos."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary material that consists of at least 50 percent material produced by inorganic chemical processes within the basin of deposition. includes inorganic síliceous, carbonate, evaporite, iron-rich, and phosphatic sediment classes."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/chemicalSedimentaryMaterial"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/chemical_sedimentary_material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/evaporita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario-ferruginoso"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/travertino"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "material sedimentario químico"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "chemical sedimentary material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-igneo"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca formada como resultado de procesos ígneos, como la intrusión y enfriamiento del magma en la corteza o las erupciones volcánicas."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Rock formed as a result of igneous processes, for example intrusion and cooling of magma in the crust, or volcanic eruption."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/igneousRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/igneous_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-doleritica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-de-composicion-exotica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-afanitica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-rica-en-vidrio"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-intermedia"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-faneritica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/porfido"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-ultrabasica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-ultramafica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca ígnea"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "igneous rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/ceniza-y-lapilli",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/tefra"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Piroclastos (o tefra) en los que menos de un 25 por ciento de los fragmentos tienen más de 64 mm de longitud."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Tephra in which less than 25 percent of fragments are greater than 64 mm in longest dimension"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/ashAndLapilli"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/ash_and_lapilli"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "ceniza y lapilli"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "ash and lapilli"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/hornblendita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-faneritica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca ultramáfica con un porcentaje superior al 40 por ciento de hornblenda más piroxeno, con una relación entre hornblenda y piroxeno mayor que 1. incluye a la hornblendita olivínica, la hornblendita olivino-piroxénica, la horblendita piroxénica y la hornblendita (s.s.)."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ultramafic rock that consists of greater than 40 percent hornblende plus pyroxene and has a hornblende to pyroxene ratio greater than 1. includes olivine hornblendite, olivine-pyroxene hornblendite, pyroxene hornblendite, and hornblendite."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/hornblendite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/hornblendite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "hornblendita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "hornblendite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/wackestone",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-carbonatada"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria carbonatada con textura original reconocible, matriz-soportada, constituida por más de un 10 por ciento de aloquímicos, en el seno de una matriz micrítica. si las partículas no son aloquímicos, su clasificación como wackestone debe ser reconsiderada."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carbonate sedimentary rock with discernible mud supported depositional texture and containing greater than 10 percent allochems, and constituent particles are of intrabasinal origin. if particles are not intrabasinal, categorization as a mudstone or wackestone should be considered."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/carbonateWackestone"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/carbonate_wackestone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "wackestone"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "carbonate wackestone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/gabroide",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-faneritica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca plutónica que contiene menos de un 90 por ciento de minerales máficos y hasta un 20 por ciento de cuarzo o un 10 por ciento de feldespatoide, entre los componentes qapf. la proporción de la plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato es mayor del 65 por ciento y el de anortita con respecto a la plagioclasa, mayor del 50 por ciento. incluye a las rocas de los sectores 9 y 10 (y sus subdivisiones) del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Phaneritic crystalline igneous rock that contains less than 90 percent mafic minerals, and up to 20 percent quartz or up to 10 percent feldspathoid in the qapf fraction. the ratio of plagioclase to total feldspar is greater than 0.65, and anorthite content of the plagioclase is greater than 50 percent. includes rocks defined modally in qapf fields 9 and 10 and their subdivisions."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/gabbroid"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/gabbroid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-monzogabroica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "gabroide"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "gabbroid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/cuarzo-sienita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sienitica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sienítica que contiene entre un 5 y un 20 por ciento de cuarzo, entre los componentes qapf. incluye a las rocas del sector 7* del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Synitic rock that contains between 5 and 20 percent quartz in the qapf fraction. defined modally in qapf field 7*."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/quartzSyenite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/quartz_syenite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "cuarzo-sienita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "quartz syenite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/traquita-de-feldespato-alcalino",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-traquitica-de-feldespato-alcalino"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca traquítica de feldespato alcalino con cuarzo, en una proporción inferior al 5 por ciento, entre los componentes qapf. sector 6 del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Trachytoid that has a plagioclase to total feldspar ratio less than 0.1, between 0 and 5 percent quartz in the qapf fraction, and no feldspathoid minerals. qapf field 6."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/alkaliFeldsparTrachyte"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/alkali_feldspar_trachyte"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "traquita de feldespato alcalino"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "alkali feldspar trachyte"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/boundstone",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-carbonatada"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria carbonatada que ha preservado su textura biogénica. sus componentes originales se unieron e incrustaron durante la sedimentación por acción de plantas y animales y se han conservado de manera sustancial en posición de vida."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary carbonate rock with preserved biogenic texture, whose original components were bound and encrusted together during deposition by the action of plants and animals during deposition, and remained substantially in the position of growth."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/boundstone"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/boundstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "boundstone"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "boundstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/pegmatita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-faneritica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca cristalina de grano excepcionalmente grueso, mayoritariamente de más de 1 cm de diámetro, con intercrecimiento de cristales; generalmente su composición es la del granito, pero se refiere a cualquier roca ígnea de grano grueso. habitualmente aparece como diques irregulares, lentejones o venas asociadas a plutones o batolitos."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Exceptionally coarse grained crystalline rock with interlocking crystals; most grains are 1cm or more diameter; composition is generally that of granite, but the term may refer to the coarse grained facies of any type of igneous rock;usually found as irregular dikes, lenses, or veins associated with plutons or batholiths."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/pegmatite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/pegmatite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "pegmatita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "pegmatite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/tefra",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-de-origen-natural-no-consolidado"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material piroclástico no consolidado que contiene un porcentaje superior al 75 por ciento de productos fragmentarios que han sido depositados como resultado directo de los procesos volcánicos y que no han sido retrabajados por procesos epiclásticos. incluye a cenizas, tefra de lapilli, tefra de bombas, tefra de bloques y aglomerados no consolidados."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Unconsolidated pyroclastic material in which greater than 75 percent of the fragments are deposited as a direct result of volcanic processes and the deposit has not been reworked by epiclastic processes. includes ash, lapilli tephra, bomb tephra, block tephra and unconsolidated agglomerate."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/tephra"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/tephra"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/ceniza-y-lapilli"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/brecha-de-cenizas"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/brecha-de-cenizas,-tefra-de-bombas-o-bloques"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "tefra"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "tephra"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-latitica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/traquitoide"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Traquitoide con una proporción entre la plagioclasa y el total de feldespato superior al 65 por ciento. sectores 8, 8' y 8* del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Trachytoid that has a plagioclase to total feldspar ratio between 0.35 and 0.65. qapf fields 8, 8' and 8*."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/latiticRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/latitic_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/latita-con-foides"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/latita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/cuarzo-latita"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca latítica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "latitic rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/arcillita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/lutita"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Lutita cuyo contenido de limos es indetectable y se considera que está formada exclusivamente por partículas de tamaño arcilla."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Mudstone that contains no detectable silt, inferred to consist virtually entirely of clay-size particles."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/claystone"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/claystone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "arcillita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "claystone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/fango-siliceo",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-pelitico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Sedimento de tamaño de grano arcilla formado por menos de un 50 por ciento de carbonatos."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Mud size sediment that consists of less than 50 percent carbonate minerals."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/silicateMud"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/silicate_mud"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "fango silíceo"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "silicate mud"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimetaria-ferruginosa",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario-ferruginoso"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria compuesta, al menos en un 50 por ciento, por minerales con hierro (hematites, magnetita, grupo de la limonita, siderita, sulfuros de hierro), determinados mediante lupa o análisis petrográfico. generalmente contiene un 15 por ciento de hierro en peso."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary rock that consists of at least 50 percent iron-bearing minerals (hematite, magnetite, limonite-group, siderite, iron-sulfides), as determined by hand-lens or petrographic analysis. corresponds to a rock typically containing 15 percent iron by weight."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/ironRichSedimentaryRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/iron_rich_sedimentary_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca sedimetaria ferruginosa"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "iron rich sedimentary rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/fosforita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario-fosfatado"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria en la que al menos el 50 por ciento de sus componentes, ya sean primarios o recristalizados, son fosfatos. habitualmente corresponde a una roca marina estratificada o retrabajada, compuesta por microcristales de fluorapatito cálcico en forma de láminas, pellets, oolitos y nódulos, y fragmentos de esqueletos, conchas y huesos."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary rock in which at least 50 percent of the primary or recrystallized constituents are phosphate minerals. most commonly occurs as a bedded primary or reworked secondary marine rock, composed of microcrystalline carbonate fluorapatite in the form of lamina, pellets, oolites and nodules, and skeletal, shell and bone fragments."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/phosphorite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/phosphorite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "fosforita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "phosphorite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento-hibrido",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/sedimento"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Sedimento que no encaja en ninguna otra categoría de sedimento según la composición o el origen. sedimento formado por tres o más componentes, cada uno de los cuales constituye entre el 5 y el 50 por ciento del material."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sediment that does not fit any of the other sediment composition/genesis categories. sediment consisting of three or more components which form more than 5 percent but less than 50 precent of the material."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/hybridSediment"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/hybrid_sediment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "sedimento híbrido"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "hybrid sediment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/granodiorita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/granitoide"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Granotoide compuesto principalmente por cuarzo, plagioclasa sódica y cantidades inferiores de feldespato alcalino, con contenidos menores de hornblenda y biotita. incluye a las rocas del sector 4 del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Phaneritic crystalline rock consisting essentially of quartz, sodic plagioclase and lesser amounts of alkali feldspar with minor hornblende and biotite. includes rocks defined modally in qapf field 4."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/granodiorite"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/granodiorite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "granodiorita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "granodiorite"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-anortositica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-faneritica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca plutónica leucocrática constituida esencialmente por plagioclasa y habitualmente con un contenido de piroxeno muy bajo. por definición, su índice de color (m) es inferior a 10 y la proporción de la plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato es mayor del 90 por ciento. contiene menos del 20 por ciento de cuarzo y del 10 por ciento de feldespatoide, entre los componentes qapf. sectores 10, 10* y 10' del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Leucocratic phaneritic crystalline igneous rock consisting essentially of plagioclase, often with small amounts of pyroxene. by definition, colour index m is less than 10, and plagiclase to total feldspar ratio is greater than 0.9. less than 20 percent quartz and less than 10 percent feldspathoid in the qapf fraction. qapf field 10, 10*, and 10'."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/anorthositicRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/anorthositic_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/anortosita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/anortosita-con-foides"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/cuarzo-anortosita"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca anortosítica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "anorthositic rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/rocas-kalsilititicas-y-melilititas",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-de-composicion-exotica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Rocas ígneas que contienen más de un 10 por ciento de kalsilita o melilita. generalmente son rocas máficas o ultramáficas, subsaturadas, ultrapotásicas (rocas kalsilitíticas) o ricas en calcio (melilititas)."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Igneous rock containing greater than 10 percent melilite or kalsilite. typically undersaturated, ultrapotassic (kalsilitic rocks) or calcium-rich (melilitic rocks) mafic or ultramafic rocks."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/kalsiliticAndMeliliticRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/kalsilitic_and_melilitic_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "rocas kalsilitíticas y melilititas"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "kalsilitic and melilitic rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/monzogabro-con-foides",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-monzogabroica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca monzogabroica con feldespatoide en una proporción inferior al 10 por ciento, entre los componentes qapf. sector 9' del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Monzogabbroic rock that contains 0 to 10 percent feldspathoid mineral in the qapf fraction. qapf field 9'."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/foidBearingMonzogabbro"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/foid_bearing_monzogabbro"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "monzogabro con foides"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "foid bearing monzogabbro"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-afanitica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca ígnea de matriz formada por cristales tan pequeños que no permiten su determinación mineralógica a simple vista; la pasta puede contener más de un 50 por ciento de vidrio. un porcentaje significativo de la roca pueden ser fenocristales. incluye a las rocas que generalmente se denominan volcánicas."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Igneous rock in which the framework of the rock consists of crystals that are too small to determine mineralogy with the unaided eye; framework may include up to 50 percent glass. a significant percentage of the rock by volume may be phenocrysts. includes rocks that are generally called volcanic rocks."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/fineGrainedIgneousRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/fine_grained_igneous_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/andesita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/foiditoide"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-volcanica-magnesica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/fonolitoide"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/tefritoide"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/traquitoide"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca afanítica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "fine grained igneous rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/carbon",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-rica-en-materia-organica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material sedimentario orgánico consolidado que tiene menos de un 75 por ciento de humedad. incluye a los carbones de rangos bajo, medio y alto según la clasificación internacional de carbones en veta (naciones unidas, 1998), por lo tanto incluye al lignito. el carbón sapropélico no se diferencia de los carbones húmicos dentro de esta denominación. se forma a partir de la compactación o el endurecimiento de restos de plantas, de manera similar a los depósitos de turba."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A consolidated organic sedimentary material having less than 75 por ciento moisture. this category includes low, medium, and high rank coals according to international classification of in-seam coal (united nations, 1998), thus including lignite. sapropelic coal is not distinguished in this category from humic coals. formed from the compaction or induration of variously altered plant remains similar to those of peaty deposits."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/coal"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/coal"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/antracita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/hulla"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/lignito"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "carbón"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "coal"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/escombro",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material de tamaños distintos originado por el derribo de edificios o antiguos revestimientos de carreteras."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Material of various size originating from broken down buildings or former road coatings."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/buildingRubble"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "escombro"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "building rubble"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-doleritica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca gabroica (basáltica) o diorítica (andesítica) oscura, de tamaño de grano intermedio entre el del basalto y el gabro, compuesta por plagioclasa, piroxeno y minerales opacos, frecuentemente con textura ofítica. típica de intrusiones hipoabisales. incluye a la dolerita, microdolerita, diabasa y el microgabro."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Dark colored gabbroic (basaltic) or dioritic (andesitic) rock intermediate in grain size between basalt and gabbro and composed of plagioclase, pyroxene and opaque minerals; often with ophitic texture. typically occurs as hypabyssal intrusions. includes dolerite, microdiorite, diabase and microgabbro."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/doleriticRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/doleritic_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca dolerítica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "doleritic rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/gabro",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-gabroica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca gabroica con cuarzo en una proporción inferior al 5 por ciento, entre los componentes qapf. incluye a las rocas del sector 10 del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Gabbroic rock that contains between 0 and 5 percent quartz and no feldspathoid mineral in the qapf fraction. includes rocks defined modally in qapf field 10 as gabbro."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/gabbro"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/gabbro"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "gabro"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "gabbro"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/lutita-organica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/lutita-generica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Lutita con un contenido elevado de carbono orgánico, normalmente querógeno. suele presentar una fina laminación y su color es marrón o negro."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Mudstone that contains a significant amount of organic carbon, typically kerogen. commonly finely laminated, brown or black in color."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/organicBearingMudstone"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/organic_bearing_mudstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "lutita orgánica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "organic bearing mudstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-de-composicion-exotica",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca con características mineralógicas, texturales o de afloramiento exóticas. típicamente oscura y con abundantes fenocristales. los criterios de inclusión son: un contenido mayor del 10 por ciento de melilita o leucita, o presencia de kalsilita, o un porcentaje superior al 50 por ciento de minerales carbonatados. incluye las carbonatitas, melilititas, rocas kalsilíticas, kimberlitas, lamproítas, leucititas y los lamprófidos."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Rock with 'exotic' mineralogical, textural or field setting characteristics; typically dark colored, with abundant phenocrysts. criteria include: presence of greater than 10 percent melilite or leucite, or presence of kalsilite, or greater than 50 percent carbonate minerals. includes carbonatite, melilitic rock, kalsilitic rocks, kimberlite, lamproite, leucitic rock and lamprophyres."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/exoticCompositionIgneousRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/exotic_composition_igneous_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/carbonatita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-alcalina-exotica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/rocas-kalsilititicas-y-melilititas"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca ígnea de composición exótica"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "exotic composition igneous rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-compuesto",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material terrestre compuesto por una agrupación de partículas de origen terrestre pudiendo incluir otros materiales compuestos."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "An earth material composed of an aggregation of particles of earth material, possibly including other compound materials."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/compoundMaterial"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/compound_material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-antropico"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/brecha"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-poligenico"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-sedimentario"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-igneo"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-no-consolidado"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "material compuesto"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "compound material"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/caliza",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-calcarea"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria carbonatada pura con una proporción entre calcita (incluyendo el aragonito) y dolomita mayor que 1. incluye a la caliza dolomítica."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Pure carbonate sedimentary rock with a calcite (plus aragonite) to dolomite ratio greater than 1 to 1. includes limestone and dolomitic limestone."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/limestone"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/limestone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/creta"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "caliza"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "limestone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/porfido",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca ígnea constituida por destacados fenocristales, en una matriz más fina, fanerítica o de grano fino."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Igneous rock that contains conspicuous phenocrysts in a finer grained groundmass; groundmass itself may be phaneritic or fine-grained."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/porphyry"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/porphyry"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "pórfido"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "porphyry"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/packstone",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-carbonatada"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria carbonatada de textura original reconocible, grano-soportada, con granos correspondientes a aloquímicos y espacios intersticiales rellenos de matriz micrítica."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carbonate sedimentary rock with discernible grain supported depositional texture, containing greater than 10 percent grains, and constituent particles are of intrabasinal origin; intergranular spaces are filled by matrix."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/packstone"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/packstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "packstone"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "packstone"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-metamorfica-foliada",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-metamorfica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca metamórfica en la que el 10 por ciento o más de los componentes minerales tienen una fábrica planar o linear. la naturaleza cataclástica o vítrea excluyen la clasificación bajo este concepto."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Metamorphic rock in which 10 percent or more of the contained mineral grains are elements in a planar or linear fabric. cataclastic or glassy character precludes classification with this concept."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/foliatedMetamorphicRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/foliated_metamorphic_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/gneis"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/filita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/esquisto"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/pizarra"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca metamórfica foliada"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "foliated metamorphic rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/alterita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-poligenico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material resultante de procesos de meteorización activos en rocas o depósitos preexistentes, análogo a las rocas hidrotermales o metasomáticas, pero formado a la temperatura y presión ambiente de la superficie de la tierra."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Material that is the product of weathering processes operating on pre-existing rocks or deposits, analogous to hydrothermal or metasomatic rocks, but formed at ambient earth surface temperature and pressure."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/materialFormedInSurficialEnvironment"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/material_formed_in_surficial_environment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/bauxita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/regolito"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Alterita"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "material formed in surficial environment"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/foidita",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
