    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/tefritoide",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-afanitica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca volcánica que contiene menos de un 90 por ciento de minerales máficos, de un 10 a un 60 por ciento de feldespatoide entre los componentes qapf y cuya proporción de plagioclasa con respecto al total de feldespato es superior al 50 por ciento. incluye a las rocas clasificadas modalmente en los sectores 13 y 14 del diagrama qapf, o químicamente en el campo u1 del diagrama tas como basanita o tefrita."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Fine grained igneous rock than contains less than 90 percent mafic minerals, between 10 and 60 percent feldspathoid mineral in the qapf fraction and has a plagioclase to total feldspar ratio greater than 0.5. includes rocks classified in qapf field 13 and 14 or chemically in tas field u1 as basanite or tephrite."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/tephritoid"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/tephritoid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/basanita"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/basanita-fonolitica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/tefrita-fonolitica"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/tefrita"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "tefritoide"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "tephritoid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/series-de-las-brechas-harinas-de-falla",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/material-relacionado-con-una-falla"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Material de falla con rasgos que indican pérdida de cohesión durante la deformación, tales como espacios vacíos (rellenos o no) o material con matriz no consolidada entre fragmentos. incluye las brechas y las harinas de falla."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Fault material with features such as void spaces (filled or unfilled), or unconsolidated matrix material between fragments, indicating loss of cohesion during deformation. includes fault-related breccia and gouge."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/breccia-gougeSeries"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/breccia_gouge_series"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "series de las brechas-harinas de falla"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "breccia-gouge series"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria-hibrida",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-sedimentaria"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca sedimentaria que no encaja en ninguna otra de las categorías de roca sedimentaria según la composición o el origen. roca sedimentaria formada por tres o más componentes, cada uno de los cuales constituye entre el 5 y el 50 por ciento del material."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sedimentary rock that does not fit any of the other composition/genesis categories. sedimentary rock consisting of three or more components which form more than 5 percent but less than 50 precent of the material."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/hybridSedimentaryRock"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/hybrid_sedimentary_rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "roca sedimentaria híbrida"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "hybrid sedimentary rock"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/gabroide-foiditico",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
        "@value": "2026-03-01"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/roca-ignea-faneritica"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "Roca plutónica en la que m es inferior a 90, con una proporción entre la plagioclasa y el total de feldespato mayor del 50 por ciento y con feldespatoide en una proporción comprendida entre el 10 y el 60 por ciento entre los componentes qapf; la plagioclasa contiene más del 50 por ciento de anortita. comúnmente presenta un elevado contenido en minerales máficos. incluye a las rocas de los sectores 13 y 14 del diagrama qapf."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Phaneritic crystalline igneous rock in which m is less than 90, the plagioclase to total feldspar ratio is greater than 0.5, feldspathoids form 10-60 percent of the qapf fraction, and plagioclase has anorthite content greater than 50 percent. these rocks typically contain large amounts of mafic minerals. includes rocks defined modally in qapf fields 13 and 14."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch": [
      {
        "@id": "http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/Lithology/foidGabbroid"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/lithology/foid_gabbroid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower": [
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/gabro-foiditico"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/monzogabro-foiditico"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "es",
        "@value": "gabroide foidítico"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "foid gabbroid"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status": [
      {
        "@value": "Válido"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/litologia/desecho",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/created": [
